    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I recently looked at the INLA slide given by David Bolin,there is the link<a href=\"http://www.math.chalmers.se/Stat/Grundutb/CTH/mve186/1415/inla_lecture.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.math.chalmers.se/Stat/Grundutb/CTH/mve186/1415/inla_lecture.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792442893986000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1DWLFDYxKpaFcVBrj7DYR5\">http://www.math.chalmers.se/Stat/Grundutb/CTH/mve186/1415/inla_lecture.pdf</a></div><div><br></div><div>In  pages 40&amp;41,the result of Tokyo Rainfall Case,give the estimate of the hyperparameters :</div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/attach/3f60f6aa92bb6/sp181015_143644.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"sp181015_143644.png\" width=\"320\" height=\"65\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\"></p><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/r-inla-discussion-group/attach/3f60f6aa92bb6/sp181015_143724.png?part=0.2&amp;view=1\" alt=\"sp181015_143724.png\" width=\"320\" height=\"193\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\"></p><div><br></div><div>Why the mean of log(tau) between 9 and 10? The result says the mean of precision for time is 20048.60,Is this not the mean of log(tau)?</div><div><br></div><div>Many thanks!</div><div>Yuki</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Zfs5NKY9BQAJ",
   "from": "Finn Lindgren",
